-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p6 A date stamp; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p7 "To"; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p8 The addressee; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p9 His post; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p10 His organisation; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p11 Its address; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p12 Its city; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p13 The subject: the early-retirement fund; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p14 The reference: the letter of 18.9.95; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p15 A greeting; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p17 The history: the 0.7% moved to the State's budget, paid straight to the funds that pay the pensions.

-- The second letter, ¶16 and ¶18: the content of the letter of 18.9.95 is
-- acceptable "in principle"; the early-retirement arrangement (0.7%) has
-- run for many years and moving it to the State did not mean to cancel the
-- allocation; but the government and the public employers may announce,
-- when agreements are renewed, that the plan is not renewed, and then the
-- parties negotiate it. So the tracks go on after תשנ"ז until such an
-- announcement and the negotiation it opens.
@ref akn:att_2__hc_1/p16 akn:att_2__hc_1/p18
GIVEN `the school year` IS A NUMBER
      `non-renewal announced on renewing the agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the early-retirement tracks stand in` `the school year` `non-renewal announced on renewing the agreements` IF
        elem `the school year` `the school years §יא keeps the early-retirement quotas in`
    OR (`the school year` AT LEAST 1997 AND NOT `non-renewal announced on renewing the agreements`)

`announcing that the early-retirement plan is not renewed` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MAY   `announce that the early-retirement plan is not renewed`
    HENCE (PARTY `the State`
           MUST  `negotiate the early-retirement plan`)

